"""
Snakefile - Wingen gene-catalog pipeline (skeleton)

Maps onto 2_wingen_create_gene_catalog.sh + filter_vcf_by_chr_or_gene.sh:

    create_gene_vcf_file()  ->  rule filter_vcf_for_gene
    extraction results     ->  checkpoint select_nonempty_genes
    create_gene_catalog()   ->  rule run_wingen_report (retained genes + optional pool)

The bash script's manual `wait -n` / max_parallel_jobs_gene_catalog_creation
loop is gone entirely. Snakemake filters genes in parallel, then waits for
all extraction/scope counts and publishes the skip report. Only after this
checkpoint does it schedule neutral preparation, retained genes' reports and
the optional All_neutral_markers report,
up to the --cores (local) or --jobs (cluster) limit. With first_gene_warmup (the
default) the first retained gene is prepared and reported alone first, with the whole
allocation; a second checkpoint (first_gene_warmup_done) makes Snakemake plan every other
gene's jobs only after that report is done.

Lives at workflow/Snakefile, the standard Snakemake project layout - run
from the REPO ROOT (not from inside workflow/), where it's auto-discovered
with no --snakefile flag needed:

    snakemake -n            # dry run
    snakemake --cores 4     # run, up to 4 genes in parallel locally

All paths below (config/config.yaml, code/..., results/...) are written
relative to the repo root for this reason - Snakemake resolves input/
output/configfile paths relative to wherever you invoke it from, not
relative to this file's own location inside workflow/.
"""

configfile: "config/config.yaml"

